# The GPUIX source update.sh builds: Kybern's fork of remorses/gpuix, whose
# `kybern` branch is the upstream release in `upstream` plus our commits. Its
# zed submodule points at Tresnanda/zed's `kybern` branch (the GPUI commits).
# A native change is a commit on those branches and a new pin here; see
# README.md, "Changing the native module".
repo=https://github.com/Tresnanda/gpuix.git
# CI triage: the heads of the forks' `ci-fix` branches: `next` (WP1 + WP10 Windows)
# plus the Linux screenshot through a wgpu readback and KYBERN_ROUNDED_CLIP=0 keeping
# edge fades, until they are merged into `kybern`; then pin the merged kybern heads.
# WP5 (notifications): the forks' `wp5` branches, one commit each on top of that.
# Second real-Windows pass: the forks' `winhw2` branches on `next` (window-state events off macOS, the window
# menu on a right click on the caption, autoFocus inside an autoFocus parent), until merged into `kybern`.
# gpuix `regressfix2`: that plus addLayoutObserver queued off macOS (no waited call per mounted row).
# `onboarding-retained`: that plus nested paintTransform scopes kept when a cached island replays inside a scope,
# and the KYBERN_PRESENT_DUMP presented-frame dump (macOS), until merged into `kybern`.
# `frame-stall`: that plus the macOS frame watchdog (a visible window without display-link frames is
# re-subscribed, its link restarted or replaced; a draw without a drawable is presented again) and
# getFrameWatchdog, until merged into `kybern`.
# `drawable-starvation`: that plus the macOS drawable gate (a draw is skipped instead of blocking in nextDrawable
# while the compositor holds every drawable; the layer is kicked) and its getFrameWatchdog fields.
# `frame-clock`: lost deliveries, acknowledgements and callback chains recover; GPUI preserves
# callbacks across failed window updates. Both forks are integrated into `next` and `kybern`.
# Background Metal drawable acquisition keeps AppKit/JS responsive even when
# nextDrawable waits below the gate's tracked queue limit. Integrated into both
# forks' `next` and `kybern` branches.
# ade96-diff-scroll: exact native diff anchors through the existing list APIs,
# including cached restores and lifecycle cleanup; no zed change.
# `kick-deadlock` (ADE-110): that plus the drawable gate's kick flushing CA transactions on a later
# main-queue turn instead of inside a draw that holds the window lock (0.20.4 deadlocked in
# resetCursorRects), AppKit display-cycle callbacks that defer instead of waiting on that lock, and
# the kick-reentry/flush-in-draw faults.
# `key-detach`: that plus no UI-thread waits per keystroke off macOS (resolveKeyEvent, subscribeAnimationFrames and
# setInputDecorations queued, the latter still validated at the call; getElementBounds answers with the last painted
# bounds without window.refresh(); Markdown and syntax documents used through a registry handle kept on the renderer)
# and stallUiThread for the checks; no zed change.
# Both are fast-forwarded into the forks' `next` and `kybern` (gpuix c9647c3, zed a2275d8, 2026-11-04):
# `commit` and `zed` are the heads of both forks' `kybern` branches.
commit=c9647c3e003b9f99eaebfa3a22ea2badbcde89da
# The zed submodule commit `commit` records; update.sh refuses a checkout that differs.
zed=a2275d84c575f48d149e8f1768248c843fc66040
# The upstream tag `commit` is based on. It must be `@gpuix/native@<VERSION>`.
upstream=@gpuix/native@0.11.0
